    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320-a1">

                <pb facs="0526" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg430"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure B—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>The Citizen President of the republic has been pleased to address me the
                    following decree:</p>
                <p>Benito Juarez, constitutional President of the United States of Mexico, to the
                    inhabitants thereof: Know ye—</p>
                <p>That the Congress of the Union has decreed as follows:</p>
                <p>The concessions granted oh the 2d of January, 1869, and the 14th of December,
                    1870, the former for the construction and management of a railroad, and the
                    latter for the construction of a canal, navigable from ocean to ocean, across
                    the Isthmus of Tehuantepec, are hereby renewed.</p>
                <pb facs="0527" n="431" xml:id="pg431"/>
                <p>The periods of time mentioned in the former shall he counted from the 2d of
                    January of the present year.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><placeName type="venue">Hall of
                                Sessions of the Congress of the Union</placeName>, <placeName
                                type="city">Mexico</placeName></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-05-22">May 22, 1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>JOSÉ H. NUNEZ,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Deputy
                        President</hi>.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>JOSÉ FERNANDEZ,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Deputy
                        Secretary</hi>.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>ENRIQUE MARIA RUBIO,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Deputy
                        Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Therefore, I order the above to be printed, published, circulated, and duly
                        obeyed.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>
                                <placeName type="venue">Palace of the Federal Government</placeName>
                                of <placeName type="city">Mexico</placeName>
                            </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1872-05-22">May 22,
                                1872</date>.</dateline>
                        <lb/>
                        <signed>BENITO JUAREZ.</signed>
                    </closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Citizen <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blas Balcárcel</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister of Public Works, Colonization, Industry,
                            and Commerce.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>And I communicate it to you for your information and consequent action.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Mexico</placeName>, <date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1872-05-22">May 22,
                            1872</date>.</dateline>
                        <lb/>
                        <signed>BALCÁRCEL.</signed>
                    </closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
